From 162e08bb68a0d9568ab879cf3d230c42397e6dfa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:33:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Search event titles and descriptions, case-insensitive

- Match is now case-insensitive
- Events that don't match by title are opened and their description is searched
- Replace XPath title lookup with plain JS so quotes (e.g. LSD 120') don't break it
- Add SEARCH_DESCRIPTION flag for fast title-only mode
- Trim the search input; abort cleanly on empty input
- Update README
---
 README.md |  18 +++-
 script.js | 255 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------------
 2 files changed, 191 insertions(+), 82 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 545388a..6ccca99 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,20 +1,30 @@
 # Google Calendar Bulk Delete
 
-Bulk delete Google Calendar events by search term. Deletes ALL events containing the entered text.
+Bulk delete Google Calendar events by search term. Deletes ALL events whose title or description contains the entered text (not case sensitive).
 
 ![Demo](demo.gif)
 
 ## Usage
 
-1. Open Google Calendar
+1. Open Google Calendar in **Month** view
 2. Run script in browser console
-3. Enter search text when prompted
+3. Enter search text when prompted (e.g. `LSD` or `AppSyncId`)
 4. Confirm deletion
 
 ## Features
 
+- Searches event titles and descriptions
+- Case-insensitive matching
 - Processes up to 12 months
 - Handles recurring events
 - Progress tracking in console
 
-**Warning:** Permanent deletion. Cannot be undone.
+## Title-only mode
+
+Searching descriptions means opening every event that does not match by title, so it is slower on busy calendars. For a fast title-only search, set this at the top of `script.js`:
+
+```js
+const SEARCH_DESCRIPTION = false;
+```
+
+**Warning:** Permanent deletion. Cannot be undone. Try a narrow search term first.
